        /// <summary>
        /// Adjust uploaded conversions Retracts, restates the value of, or enhances conversions you already sent to Google Ads, Impact or a Microsoft Ads offline conversion goal, for refunds or late customer data. To change Zernio&#39;s stored event too, and every platform at once, use &#x60;PATCH&#x60; or &#x60;DELETE /v1/events/{eventId}&#x60;.  It adjusts conversions previously uploaded via &#x60;POST /v1/ads/conversions&#x60;: retract them, restate their value, or enhance them with first-party data. Requires the Ads add-on.  ### Google Ads, Impact and Microsoft Ads only  Google handles adjustments through the classic Google Ads API (&#x60;ConversionAdjustmentUploadService&#x60;). The Data Manager &#x60;ingestEvents&#x60; path used for sending conversions is ingest-only.  On Impact, the partner&#39;s commission follows the refund:  - &#x60;RETRACTION&#x60; reverses the action and &#x60;RESTATEMENT&#x60; sets its sale amount. Impact has no &#x60;ENHANCEMENT&#x60;. - The action is found by the &#x60;destinationId&#x60; event type and &#x60;orderId&#x60;: the &#x60;platformData.order_id&#x60; the conversion was sent with, or its &#x60;eventId&#x60; when it had none. - Impact applies changes asynchronously and refuses them on its side past the action&#39;s locking date.  On Microsoft Ads (&#x60;ApplyOfflineConversionAdjustments&#x60;), only offline conversion goals take changes; a UET tag refuses them:  - &#x60;RETRACTION&#x60; retracts the conversion and &#x60;RESTATEMENT&#x60; sets its new value. Microsoft has no &#x60;ENHANCEMENT&#x60;. - Microsoft has no order id: send &#x60;msclkid&#x60; and &#x60;conversionTime&#x60;, the click id and time the conversion was sent with.  Other platforms have no equivalent, so this endpoint returns &#x60;405&#x60; for them.  ### Adjustment types  - &#x60;RETRACTION&#x60;: remove the conversion entirely (refund, chargeback, cancelled order, churn). - &#x60;RESTATEMENT&#x60;: change the conversion&#39;s value (upgrade / downgrade / partial refund). Send the corrected **total** value in &#x60;restatementValue&#x60; (not a delta). - &#x60;ENHANCEMENT&#x60;: attach first-party identifiers (hashed email / phone) to an existing conversion (enhanced conversions applied after the fact).  ### Identifying the original conversion  Per adjustment, send one of:  - &#x60;orderId&#x60;: the transaction ID you sent as &#x60;eventId&#x60; on the original conversion. Recommended, and **required** for &#x60;ENHANCEMENT&#x60;. - &#x60;gclid&#x60; + &#x60;conversionTime&#x60;: the click ID and the original conversion&#39;s time (unix seconds). Not available for &#x60;ENHANCEMENT&#x60;. - &#x60;msclkid&#x60; + &#x60;conversionTime&#x60;: the only key on Microsoft Ads.  ### Other fields  - &#x60;destinationId&#x60; is the same value you send to &#x60;POST /v1/ads/conversions&#x60;: the conversion action resource name on Google, e.g. &#x60;customers/1234567890/conversionActions/987654321&#x60;, &#x60;&lt;program id&gt;:&lt;event type id&gt;&#x60; on Impact, and &#x60;accounts/{adAccountId}/conversionGoals/{goalId}&#x60; on Microsoft Ads. - PII in &#x60;user&#x60; is hashed with SHA-256 server-side (Gmail-specific normalization included). Send plaintext. - Times are unix seconds; we convert to Google&#39;s required &#x60;yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm:ss+00:00&#x60; format.  ### Limits  Up to 2000 adjustments per request. Partial failure is supported (inspect &#x60;adjustmentsFailed&#x60; / &#x60;failures[]&#x60;). 
