        /// <summary>
        /// Send events to every destination The recommended way to send conversions. Sends conversion events once and forwards them to every ad platform destination saved for the profile (see &#x60;POST /v1/events/destinations&#x60;), or to the &#x60;destinations&#x60; given in the request. Requires the Ads add-on.  ### Forwarding  - Each destination receives the events exactly as &#x60;POST /v1/ads/conversions&#x60; would send them, so the per-platform notes there (hashing, batching, &#x60;eventName&#x60; semantics, dedup on &#x60;eventId&#x60;) apply here too. - A destination saved with &#x60;eventNames&#x60; only receives events with those names. - One destination failing never blocks the others: each one reports its own result.  ### Consent  Send each visitor&#39;s consent on the event (&#x60;events[].consent&#x60;) or for the whole request (&#x60;consent&#x60;), as Google Consent Mode&#39;s four signals. Zernio applies it per destination for visitors in the EEA, the UK and Switzerland, read from &#x60;user.country&#x60; (website events use the visitor&#39;s country):  - A signal left out counts as &#x60;DENIED&#x60;. Zernio has no setting to change this. - Meta, LinkedIn, TikTok, Pinterest, Reddit, X, Snapchat, Microsoft, OpenAI and AppLovin get the event only with &#x60;adUserData: GRANTED&#x60; and neither &#x60;adStorage&#x60; nor &#x60;adPersonalization&#x60; &#x60;DENIED&#x60;. - Google Ads gets every event with &#x60;adUserData&#x60; and &#x60;adPersonalization&#x60; set, a missing one as &#x60;DENIED&#x60;. Google decides what it can use. - Google Analytics gets the event only with &#x60;analyticsStorage: GRANTED&#x60;, with the same ad signals. - An event left out is reported on its destination as &#x60;drops&#x60; (with &#x60;consent_denied&#x60; or &#x60;consent_missing&#x60;), as &#x60;dropped&#x60; on &#x60;GET /v1/events/{eventId}&#x60;, and counted in &#x60;GET /v1/events/overview&#x60;. It is still stored and counted in your results. - Visitors elsewhere, or with no &#x60;user.country&#x60;, are sent as before with the consent they carry.  Zernio applies the consent you send; it does not collect it or give legal advice. Profiles created before this rule started (Nov 2026) keep sending as before until they are switched over.  ### Storage  Zernio also stores each event for the profile&#39;s reporting.  - Email, phone and &#x60;externalId&#x60; are stored only as SHA-256 hashes. - &#x60;sourceUrl&#x60; keeps only its origin, path and attribution parameters (&#x60;utm_*&#x60;, &#x60;zrn&#x60;, &#x60;zcid&#x60;, &#x60;gclid&#x60;, &#x60;gbraid&#x60;, &#x60;wbraid&#x60;, &#x60;fbclid&#x60;, &#x60;ttclid&#x60;, &#x60;twclid&#x60;, &#x60;msclkid&#x60;, &#x60;li_fat_id&#x60;, &#x60;epik&#x60;, &#x60;rdt_cid&#x60;, &#x60;oppref&#x60;, &#x60;aleid&#x60;, &#x60;alart&#x60;), each also under a &#x60;z&#x60;-prefixed copy such as &#x60;zgclid&#x60;. - Events sent with &#x60;testCode&#x60; are forwarded but not stored. - Sending an event again with the same &#x60;eventId&#x60; replaces the stored one. - A stored &#x60;Purchase&#x60;, &#x60;Lead&#x60; or &#x60;QualifiedLead&#x60; tied to one of your campaigns (see &#x60;campaign&#x60; on each event) counts in &#x60;GET /v1/ads/campaign-results&#x60; and in ad rules as &#x60;sales&#x60; and &#x60;revenue&#x60;, &#x60;leads&#x60; or &#x60;qualified_leads&#x60;. 
